y NCBI home page by  clicking manage collections merge and  delete are only available for custom  collections meaning that favorites my  bibliography and other citations cannot  be merged or deleted also you are able  to check the date less modified by  hovering over the text this concludes  the brief tutorial on how to create an  automated search create a collection and  activate a public URL if there are any  remaining questions please feel free to  ask them at this time and thank you once  again for joining us  ok thanks sherry there was one question  in the chat box that I didn't answer is  it not possible to  order collection to EndNote is the  question that I see here you are not  able to do it in your personalized  customized collection however you are  able to do it in either my bibliography  or other other citations there is a link  after after the questions which will  give you a step-by-step on how to export  from those collections meaning my  bibliography or other other citations  another question is is there a way to  automatically save collections as PDFs  not at this time but that is actually a  really great suggestion that we will  pass on okay thank you I don't have any  other questions in the questions pod  Cheri's showing the last slide here this  is some additional documents that you  might find helpful there's a two minute  PubMed search tutorials available here  and there is a youtube video on using my  bibliography and other citations and  just to remind you to keep up with NCBI  you can check in at our NCBI insights  blog of URLs given there NCBI insights  that NCBI NLM NIH gov and we do have a  YouTube channel  in CBI NLM is the username there so just  look for that on YouTube and for any  questions about help with NCBI resources  please write to info info at NCBI  NLM NIH gov if you have specific  questions about the webinars program  write to webinars its webinars at NCBI  NLM NIH stubb thanks everyone for coming  you
 

